+# R50 — DIANWEI 8.21A0.024200 J3 candidate evaluation
+
+Status: **EVALUATION ONLY — do not replace PCB J3 until footprint and mating verification**. Base source remains on R49/R48 routing with J3 Hirose FH34SRJ-24S-0.5SH. No copper is qualified by this note.
+
+## Supplier evidence
+Good Display supplied `24pin双接触 连接器.pdf` for the 8.21A0 family, describing the **8.21A0.024200** 24-position / 0.5 mm pitch / dual-contact / nominal 1.2 mm height connector. Source reference and SHA256 are recorded in `hardware/mainboard/research/GOODDISPLAY_REPLY_2026-10-09.md`. The supplied document is a **drawing-derived candidate**, not explicit Good Display approval of this item for GDEY0397T81P. Do not commit supplier PDF to this public repository without permission.
+
+Hirose incumbent: FH34SRJ-24S-0.5SH, 24-way, 0.5 mm, 1.0 mm height, 14.0 mm length, 3.8 mm width, both top and bottom contact, rear-flip ZIF, horizontal insertion, 0.30 mm nominal FPC thickness. Manufacturer: https://www.hirose.com/en/product/p/CL0580-1255-6-99
+
+## Decision matrix
+| Check | Hirose FH34SRJ | DIANWEI 8.21A0.024200 | Action |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Number of contacts | 24 | 24 according to vendor drawing | match count only |
+| Pitch | 0.50 mm | 0.50 mm according to vendor drawing | match pitch only |
+| Contact side | top and bottom | dual-sided according to vendor drawing | no inherent advantage over Hirose |
+| Height | 1.0 mm | 1.2 mm per vendor drawing | update enclosure clearance |
+| Pad / hold-down geometry | Hirose-specific | different mechanical drawing | **NOT footprint compatible** without full pad-centroid overlay |
+| FPC thickness / insertion depth | 0.30 mm / manufacturer drawing | **unverified** against exact production FPC | confirm with datasheet and sample |
+| Latch and access | rear-flip ZIF | evaluate supplier drawing | check user assembly / chassis access |
+| Pin 1 / insertion / mirrored map | must verify physical orientation | must verify physical orientation | explicit top/bottom + back view checklist |
+| Polish procurement and prototype stock | distributor options for Hirose | exact P/N major-distributor listing not confirmed in current public search | ask Good Display / DIANWEI for source, MOQ, 10 pcs |
+| Vendor mating endorsement | unconfirmed | unconfirmed | demand explicit GDEY0397T81P mating confirmation |
+
+## PCB implementation gate
+1. Extract actual connector drawing's PCB land pattern, SMT locating tabs, tolerances, actuator sweep, and body outline; measure pad centres against original J3 Hirose KiCad footprint.
+2. Validate panel FPC contact side, pin-1 mark, contact-tail width/thickness, stiffener and insertion depth; also bend clearance in real panel orientation and 3D case.
+3. Only then duplicate the existing footprint into project library with a new `DIANWEI_8.21A0.024200` name, **without silently reusing the Hirose pad geometry**. Match all 24 nets pad-by-pad against current schematic and EPD PDF; inspect mirrored footprint in front/back CAD.
+4. Create a placement / routing comparison on a separate PCB revision, rerun ERC and full Native KiCad DRC, mechanical overlay and BOM/PNP. Confirm actual assembler availability and purchasing channel.
+5. **Pin5 VDHR / VSH2 remains an independent hard electrical HOLD**. No manufacturing release while vendor's current panel map is contradictory.
+6. **No fabricated sample** and full PCB routing/DRC remains incomplete (R48: 139 unrouted, 168 other DRC). Do not infer production readiness from a connector selection.
+
+Recommendation: retain the proven original J3 as baseline, evaluate DIANWEI as second-source or mechanical improvement. The Hirose is already dual-contact, so DIANWEI is not automatically a functional upgrade. Before physical replacement require approved dimensioned land pattern, FPC sample fit and traceable procurement.
+
+Readiness: **44/100, PCBWay NO-GO**, unchanged; no PCB copper modification in R50 candidate intake.
